{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/357679-looking-for-an-explanation-for-titanspawn-god-distinction","id":357679,"title":"Looking for an explanation for Titanspawn/God distinction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-02T13:12:23-08:00","id":357679,"title":"Looking for an explanation for Titanspawn/God distinction","content":"So I'm trying to make my own RP universe based on the Scion universe, and i'm trying to make sense of things. I've got most of the things sorted, with some Avatars being old-generation Gods turned to Titan Avatars (Kronus, Apep...) through too many Fatebindings (explaining why the Gods fear Fate), with other being older, more primordial beings (Nut, Gaia...)The problem is that Titans give birth to Titanspawn, so why do they also spawn Gods ? What's special about Gods that makes them different from Titanspawn ? Why are there so few of them compared to the legions of Titanspawn ? Why are Titanspawn faithful to the Titans but Gods arn't ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3865-rwandrall","name":"Rwandrall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:57:48-08:00","id":357998,"title":"","content":"The distinction's not explicitly stated (Titanspawn is mainly just Scion's term for &quot;all those creatures what the Gods and their kids fight&quot; so that's a large umbrella). From what I remember from God and a bit from Ragnarok, the gods WERE Titanspawn, or Titans, once upon a time. Then they started interacting with humanity. Interacting with mortals caused Fatebindings that replaced the more subservient Dark Virtues with regular ol' Virtues. The Titanspawn who became Gods are the ones that started giving a shit about humanity and the world in general. There's more to it than that, and the difference as far as pantheons or individual gods can vary greatly, but that's the gist of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T22:00:17-08:00","id":358040,"title":"","content":"There are actually two distinctions. The original Titanspawn were created solely from a single Greater Titan - Surtr coming from only Muspelheim, for example. The Gods were born from the friction between two or more Greater Titans. Over time things changed, with some gods becoming titanspawn and vice versa, but the main thing is that Gods have their own will and minds, whereas the Titanspawn are all aspects of the Greater Titan's consciousness. When gods become titanspawn, they lose their own free will and become aspects of the greater titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4311-sparky-young-upstart","name":"Sparky Young Upstart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T12:19:06-08:00","id":359393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rwandrall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/357679-looking-for-an-explanation-for-titanspawn-god-distinction#post357679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm trying to make my own RP universe based on the Scion universe, and i'm trying to make sense of things. I've got most of the things sorted, with some Avatars being old-generation Gods turned to Titan Avatars (Kronus, Apep...) through too many Fatebindings (explaining why the Gods fear Fate), with other being older, more primordial beings (Nut, Gaia...)The problem is that Titans give birth to Titanspawn, so why do they also spawn Gods ? What's special about Gods that makes them different from Titanspawn ? Why are there so few of them compared to the legions of Titanspawn ? Why are Titanspawn faithful to the Titans but Gods arn't ?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going by the book, then the above responses will do.<br /> I myself don't really follow the books, or even a lot of the pantheons. Some of the Titans as scrutinized in Greek sources weren't really bad. Indeed, they were a necessary part of the universe.<br /> And that's how I usually see it;<br /> Some titans bad, some good.<br /> Some gods bad, some good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:16:52-08:00","id":361378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sparky Young Upstart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/357679-looking-for-an-explanation-for-titanspawn-god-distinction?p=358040#post358040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are actually two distinctions. The original Titanspawn were created solely from a single Greater Titan - Surtr coming from only Muspelheim, for example. The Gods were born from the friction between two or more Greater Titans. Over time things changed, with some gods becoming titanspawn and vice versa, but the main thing is that Gods have their own will and minds, whereas the Titanspawn are all aspects of the Greater Titan's consciousness. When gods become titanspawn, they lose their own free will and become aspects of the greater titan.</div> </div> </div> </div>This basically. Titanspawn are all the minion critters that inhabit/worship/obey the Titan. Titan Avatars are big guys comparable to Gods. When a Titan reproduces with itself, it makes Titan Avatar - so Surtr and all the Fire avatars are only Fire domain. When a titan reproduces with a different titan, you get a mixture that becomes a God.<br /> <br /> What I think is the most interesting bit isn't origin. It's the &quot;when an Avatar calls on max power, it's self dissolves back into the titan. When a God does, it becomes a weird thing for a scene then goes back to normal.&quot; So there's kind this thing where avatars have protection from Mama, but less power and free will, while Gods are on their own (barring forming a pantheon) but can summon universal cosmic power. The tension between those two would drive Avatars wanting to become Gods and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T08:06:17-08:00","id":364412,"title":"","content":"Personally? I'd have to say the distinction is their personalities and intelligence. From what we can tell, the Titans and their spawn are forces of nature who don't really have a grasp of human concepts. Gods, on the other hand, are much more human in their actions and are more comprehensible. If a Titan Spawn managed to obtain some degree of humanity, it's possible they could become classified as a new God, and likewise if a God loses touch with humanity, they might become a Titan Spawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}